{
  "date": "2026-11-22",
  "pillar": "Technology & Architecture",
  "headline": "Your client will retry. Make sure your API only charges once.",
  "slides": [
    {
      "theme": "dark",
      "tag": "Architecture · Distributed systems",
      "offset": 180,
      "html": "<h1>Your client will retry.</h1><h1 class='accent' style='margin-top:28px;font-size:92px'>Make sure your API only charges once.</h1><p style='margin-top:56px;max-width:820px'>Retries are not an edge case. They are how distributed systems survive. Duplicates are what happens when nobody designed for them.</p>",
      "footnote": "swipe →"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Context",
      "offset": 130,
      "html": "<div class='kicker'>A timeout is not an answer</div><h2>The client waited 30 seconds. Then it gave up.</h2><p>What actually happened on the server? From the client’s side, there is no way to know.</p><hr style='margin:30px 0'><p style='font-size:32px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>A</span>&nbsp; The request never arrived.</p><p style='font-size:32px;margin-top:14px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>B</span>&nbsp; It succeeded. The response was lost.</p><p style='font-size:32px;margin-top:14px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>C</span>&nbsp; It is still running.</p><hr style='margin:30px 0'><p>The only sensible move is to retry. In case B, a naive retry charges the customer twice.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "The concept",
      "offset": 150,
      "html": "<h2>Idempotent: doing it twice has the same effect as doing it once.</h2><p>Reading a record is naturally idempotent. So is “set status to shipped”.</p><hr><p>“Create a charge” is not. Each call is a new charge, unless the API can recognise a repeat.</p><hr><p style='color:#0E0E0E'>Networks deliver <span class='mono' style='font-size:30px'>at least once</span>. Make the handler idempotent and the business outcome happens <span class='accent'>exactly once</span>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "How it works",
      "offset": 90,
      "html": "<h2 style='margin-bottom:30px'>The idempotency key</h2><svg width='850' height='800' viewBox='0 0 850 800'><g font-family='Plex Mono'><rect x='10' y='0' width='220' height='64' fill='none' stroke='#0E0E0E' stroke-width='2'/><text x='120' y='42' font-size='26' fill='#0E0E0E' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='500'>Client</text><rect x='620' y='0' width='220' height='64' fill='none' stroke='#0E0E0E' stroke-width='2'/><text x='730' y='42' font-size='26' fill='#0E0E0E' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='500'>API</text><line x1='120' y1='64' x2='120' y2='680' stroke='#D4D4D0' stroke-width='2'/><line x1='730' y1='64' x2='730' y2='680' stroke='#D4D4D0' stroke-width='2'/><text x='425' y='122' font-size='23' fill='#0E0E0E' text-anchor='middle'>POST /charges · key a1f9</text><line x1='120' y1='140' x2='716' y2='140' stroke='#0E0E0E' stroke-width='2'/><polygon points='730,140 712,131 712,149' fill='#0E0E0E'/><rect x='300' y='170' width='420' height='76' fill='#2F5FE8' fill-opacity='0.08' stroke='#2F5FE8' stroke-width='2'/><text x='510' y='202' font-size='22' fill='#2F5FE8' text-anchor='middle'>charge once, then save</text><text x='510' y='232' font-size='22' fill='#2F5FE8' text-anchor='middle'>key + response together</text><line x1='134' y1='330' x2='730' y2='330' stroke='#6B6B6B' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='10 8'/><polygon points='120,330 138,321 138,339' fill='#6B6B6B'/><text x='425' y='310' font-size='23' fill='#6B6B6B' text-anchor='middle'>response lost · timeout</text><text x='425' y='341' font-size='34' fill='#6B6B6B' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='500'>✕</text><text x='425' y='432' font-size='23' fill='#0E0E0E' text-anchor='middle'>retry · same key a1f9</text><line x1='120' y1='450' x2='716' y2='450' stroke='#0E0E0E' stroke-width='2'/><polygon points='730,450 712,441 712,459' fill='#0E0E0E'/><rect x='300' y='480' width='420' height='76' fill='#2F5FE8' fill-opacity='0.08' stroke='#2F5FE8' stroke-width='2'/><text x='510' y='512' font-size='22' fill='#2F5FE8' text-anchor='middle'>key seen: skip the work,</text><text x='510' y='542' font-size='22' fill='#2F5FE8' text-anchor='middle'>return the saved response</text><text x='425' y='610' font-size='23' fill='#0E0E0E' text-anchor='middle'>200 · same charge id</text><line x1='134' y1='628' x2='730' y2='628' stroke='#0E0E0E' stroke-width='2'/><polygon points='120,628 138,619 138,637' fill='#0E0E0E'/><text x='0' y='750' font-size='26' fill='#2F5FE8' font-weight='500'>Two requests. One charge.</text><text x='0' y='790' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>The key identifies the intent, not the attempt.</text></g></svg>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Real-world example",
      "offset": 140,
      "html": "<div class='kicker'>Stripe’s API</div><h2>Payments APIs have shipped this for years.</h2><p style='font-size:32px'>Stripe accepts an <span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>Idempotency-Key</span> header on POST requests. In its v1 API:</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p style='font-size:32px'>A retry with the same key gets the saved first response, even if that was an error.</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p style='font-size:32px'>Reuse a key with different parameters and the request is rejected.</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p style='font-size:32px'>Keys can be pruned after 24 hours. After that, the same key is a new request.</p><p class='mono' style='margin-top:30px;font-size:22px;color:#6B6B6B'>Source: docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Practical application",
      "offset": 110,
      "html": "<h2>Building it into your own API</h2><div style='display:flex;gap:28px;margin-bottom:26px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:30px;line-height:1.45;flex:none'>01</span><p style='font-size:31px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Client creates the key</b> once per user action, and reuses it on every retry.</p></div><div style='display:flex;gap:28px;margin-bottom:26px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:30px;line-height:1.45;flex:none'>02</span><p style='font-size:31px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Save atomically.</b> Key, request hash and result in the same transaction as the side effect.</p></div><div style='display:flex;gap:28px;margin-bottom:26px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:30px;line-height:1.45;flex:none'>03</span><p style='font-size:31px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Handle in-flight repeats.</b> Same key still processing? Return a conflict, not a second run.</p></div><div style='display:flex;gap:28px'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:30px;line-height:1.45;flex:none'>04</span><p style='font-size:31px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Outlive the retries.</b> Keep keys longer than any client, queue or webhook will retry.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Takeaways",
      "offset": 140,
      "html": "<h2>Three mistakes to avoid</h2><p class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B;letter-spacing:.06em'>MISTAKE</p><p style='font-size:34px;color:#0E0E0E'>A new key for every attempt.</p><p style='font-size:30px;margin-top:6px'>That makes every retry look new.</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B;letter-spacing:.06em'>MISTAKE</p><p style='font-size:34px;color:#0E0E0E'>Check first, write later.</p><p style='font-size:30px;margin-top:6px'>Two parallel retries both pass the check.</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B;letter-spacing:.06em'>MISTAKE</p><p style='font-size:34px;color:#0E0E0E'>Only protecting the API.</p><p style='font-size:30px;margin-top:6px'>Queue consumers and webhooks redeliver too.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "dark",
      "tag": "Your turn",
      "offset": 190,
      "html": "<h2 style='font-size:76px'>Which operation in your system would hurt most if it ran twice?</h2><p style='margin-top:30px'>A payment, an email, a stock update, a provisioning job?</p><hr><p class='mono' style='font-size:28px;line-height:1.8'><span class='accent'>Save</span> this for your next API design review.<br><span class='accent'>Follow</span> @techtaleswithabhi for delivery, architecture &amp; AI — without the hype.</p>",
